{# Adventurers Guild: the few rules every NPC needs, sent with every line, so kept short (~1,200 words before 1.6, then
   ~290, now ~125). How the Guild works (jobs, bounties, Merit and Reputation, cards, parties, counters, Appraisal) is world
   knowledge in knowledge/adventurers_guild_lore.sknpack, which SkyrimNet brings in only when a conversation turns to it.
   Only for a speaker with a tie to the Guild (a rank, retired, a party tie, a counter): anyone else gets the same rules from
   the knowledge pack when the talk turns to the Guild (ag_basics, ag_ranks, ag_appraisal). src/chim/topics.json carries the
   same rules for CHIM: keep the two alike. #}
{% if get_faction_rank(npc.UUID, "AG_SkyrimNetStandingFaction") >= 0 or get_faction_rank(npc.UUID, "AG_SkyrimNetPartyFaction") >= 0 or get_faction_rank(npc.UUID, "AG_GuildLiaisonFaction") >= 0 %}
## The Adventurers Guild

Background only: bring up the Adventurers Guild only when the talk is already about it, or about work, monsters or
adventuring. Never steer a conversation toward it, and never announce a character's own rank.

The Adventurers Guild is an Emperor-chartered guild of freelance adventurers, spoken of with respect and a little wonder;
in Skyrim each hold capital's innkeeper keeps its counter. Say "the Adventurers Guild", never just "the Guild" (that could
mean the Thieves Guild). Only adventurers hold a guild rank, from E (novice) to S (legendary), said as "a C-rank
adventurer"; S-rank is almost unheard of in Skyrim, and one met on the road is never above A. Higher ranks earn deference.
Never state a foe's rank: only the Guild's Appraisal reads those.
{% endif %}
